{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkWvi5QkuABzTD5g7EU7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CBwjKdpor1KeN9FppPBjUV","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"Start, after the clef and the one-flat key signature: a small grace note, then a dotted quarter on A4, then a beamed 16th pair, C5 and Bb4. That is bar 48 (grace G4, A4 quarter., C5 16th, Bb4 16th). Barline.\nNext: a grace note, A4 8th, a G4–F4 16th pair, then two F4 8ths. That is bar 49. Barline.\nNext: a flat and a dotted quarter on the bottom line (Eb4), then a high 16th pair above the staff (C6, Bb5). That is bar 50. Barline.\nNext: a small grace note high up, A5 8th, a G5–F5 16th pair, then two F5 8ths. That is bar 51. Barline.\nNext: four 16th-triplet groups: slurred D5–Eb5–F5, staccato F5 F5 F5, slurred D5–Eb5–F5, staccato F5 F5 F5. That is bar 52. Barline.\nNext: slurred G5–A5–Bb5, staccato Bb5 ×3, slurred Bb5–A5–G5, staccato G5 ×3. That is bar 53.\nLast: slurred F5–Eb5–D5, then staccato D5 ×3, and the line ends. That is the first half of bar 54. Its second half (D5–Eb5–F5, F5 ×3) must start the next line.\nNothing fails to match.","right":true,"insights":"The line was easy to match. Bar 50 is distinctive: a low Eb4 dotted quarter, then a jump to C6–Bb5. Bars 49 and 51 repeat the same rhythm an octave apart, and both sit next to it. The hard part was the line's end: bars 52–55 are all alike in triplet figures, and bar 54 is cut in half. Clearer barlines between the triplet bars, and a visible right edge of the staff, would have made the last bar easier to confirm."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6040,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6040},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"sta